{"id": 34, "ts": 1780489364.6338074, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is our best provisional choice.\u202fJames confirmed C\u2019s calmness in a crisis and rapid, correct decision\u2011making, while my notes add that C is 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere\u2014covering operational reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and crew cooperation.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fA does show impressive technical traits (anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, excellent spatial vision) and strong leadership qualities, but we have no evidence of his stress\u2011resilience or consistent reliability, which are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fCandidate\u202fD, although responsible and attentive, is described as arrogant, a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d with a hot temper and weak leadership, raising serious doubts about crew cooperation and communication.\u202fThus, given the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC still offers the most balanced safety\u2011critical profile."}
